<%# Create, on the same shape as the record page.

    **`max-w-3xl`, not `max-w-7xl`.** Measured at 1366px: this form was 1062px wide while the same school's
    edit page was 768px, for the same single name field. design.md already records that defect on
    `classrooms#edit` - "a form's measure does not scale with the window" - and this page had it.

    **One section, and it says why.** A school that does not exist yet cannot have school years: there is no
    id to attach a `SchoolYear` to. So create shows the attributes only, and names what comes next rather
    than leaving the difference unexplained. That is the create-then-configure flow Stripe and Shopify admin
    both use - a minimal create, then the record's own page. %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "New school",
                       description: "You will add its school years after it exists." } do %><% end %>

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <section aria-labelledby="details-heading">
      <h2 id="details-heading" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Details</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">The only thing a new school needs.</p>

      <div class="mt-3">
        <%= render "form" %>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
